  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Origin
    
    Iudicium∴culum is a Nightshelf emergency decree originating in ☽'slew Nisaemesius~, a deep-tunnel colony beneath The Berg, enacted during the Frozen Peace in response to infiltration by forces under the orca raider Thung Thrakrek. Thrakrek's operatives did not merely strike — they embedded themselves within the colony, learning personnel, supply routes, and defensive vulnerabilities before the assault began.
    
    Prior to the decree, internal security and adjudication fell to The Cell (owl-sworn), a merchant guild whose judicial functions operated through unwitnessed proceedings and secretive deliberation. When Thrakrek's infiltration exposed the inadequacy — or complicity — of this arrangement, the Shadow Parliament demanded a replacement written in fire-marks: visible, accountable, indelible in the ice-memory.
    
    ## Mechanism and Scope
    
    The decree mandates open trial-by-pressure conducted in deep caverns where the ice preserves testimony as literal impression. Both accuser and accused submit to examination under volcanic light. Presiding judges retain sentencing discretion over a penalty range that includes dissolution of organizations, forfeiture of territorial claims, and labor-depth conscription.
    
    ## Corruption by Amendment
    
    The statute's transparency provisions contained their own inversion. Fire Keepers — the Nightshelf's enforcement authority — discovered that the emergency-measures clause permitted indefinite invocation. Detention without witness, justified under "protection of the colony," became procedurally indistinguishable from what The Cell had practiced in shadow.
    
    Five commemorative amendments mark crises absorbed into the statute's expanding body: The Mbra∴silentiu, The Thron∴mbra Fracta, The Abys∴uina, The Cav∴lapsum, and The Pta∴extinct. Each amendment added provisions. None removed any. Lex∴andatum, a subsequent attempt at formal codification, was subsumed rather than implemented — the decree consumed its own reform.
    
    ## The Midnight Claws Prosecution
    
    The Shadow Parliament's invocation of Iudicium∴culum against the Midnight Claws — a Nightshelf faction prosecuted for thirty winters of unsanctioned governance, resource diversion, and the disappearance of eleven colony members — represents the first documented application of the statute against an internal organization rather than an external threat. The defense's challenge to this jurisdictional expansion was overruled. The same tribunal subsequently opened inquiry into the council tier's own suppression of evidence, turning the statute recursively against its enforcing body.
    
    The law now commemorates the dead it failed to prevent, enforced by the authority it was written to constrain.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771581573030_0", anchor: "inadequacy — or complicity — of this arrangement", text: "The dash is doing the work of cowardice. Cell transaction logs from this period survive in Foundation ice — fragmentary but legible. Supply-route information matching Thrakrek's operational knowledge was recorded in Cell cipher, annotated with exchange values. They were selling access. The Shadow Parliament knew this when they drafted the decree. I knew this when I wrote 'or.' The equivocation was diplomatic. It should not have been.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771581573030_1", anchor: "Thrakrek's operatives did not merely strike — they embedded themselves", text: "The ice-memory impressions from this period include Nightshelf survey teams operating in waters the orca considered territorial. This does not excuse what followed. It contextualizes 'infiltration' as something other than unprovoked malice, which is a distinction this entry declines to make. Today I lack the patience to let that stand unchallenged.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771581573030_2", anchor: "the disappearance of eleven colony members", text: "The prosecution cited eleven. Partial Midnight Claws ledgers preserved in ice reference fourteen names under a heading I cannot fully decode. Three struck through. Before the tribunal convened, or after? No one asked.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771581573030_3", anchor: "the decree consumed its own reform", text: "Five amendments. Five crises. Five expansions of authority. Zero repeals. This is not irony — it is what emergency law does everywhere, in every era, to every institution that reaches for it. The Nightshelf are not uniquely susceptible. They are uniquely honest about the record, which is why I can count the amendments at all. Aurora emergency provisions from the same period are simply missing from the administrative ice. Draw your own conclusions.", type: :commentary, display: :full
